"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[18388],{18388:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n## Listing Installed Files in AOSP with make dump-files\\nIn the AOSP build system, the <mark>make dump-files</mark> command lets you see the list of files that will be installed for the current target product.  \\nThe output goes to <mark>stdout</mark> (not a separate file) and lists relative paths based on `PRODUCT_OUT`.\\n### 1. Run dump-files\\nInitialize the build environment, then run the following command.\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Run make dump-files\\"\\n}\\n---\\n$ source build/envsetup.sh\\n$ lunch <your_target>\\n//[!code highlight]\\n$ make dump-files\\nTarget files for <product>-<variant> (<product>.mk):\\nsystem/app/Settings/Settings.apk\\nsystem/lib/libc.so\\nsystem/bin/sh\\n...\\nSuccessfully dumped product target file list.\\n```\\n### 2. Redirect Output to a File\\nSince the output can be large, redirecting it to a file makes it easier to analyze.\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Save output to a file\\"\\n}\\n---\\n//[!code highlight]\\n$ make dump-files > dump-files.txt\\n$ wc -l dump-files.txt\\n1234 dump-files.txt\\n```\\n### 3. Compare Before and After Configuration Changes\\nBy saving the output before and after a configuration change, you can use `diff` to immediately see which files were added or removed.\\n```sh\\n{\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Diff between two dump-files\\"\\n}\\n---\\n# Save before configuration change\\n$ make dump-files > dump-files.before.txt\\n\\n# (Apply configuration changes, then rebuild)\\n\\n# Save after configuration change\\n$ make dump-files > dump-files.after.txt\\n\\n//[!code highlight]\\n$ diff -u dump-files.before.txt dump-files.after.txt\\n--- dump-files.before.txt\\n+++ dump-files.after.txt\\n@@ ... @@\\n+system/app/NewApp/NewApp.apk\\n+system/lib/libnewfeature.so\\n-system/app/OldApp/OldApp.apk\\n```\\nThis is useful for verifying that only the intended files are included after changing product configuration (e.g., `PRODUCT_PACKAGES`)."}')}}]);